PART 3 — Functional Home Screen Download Button

3.1 Existing implementation

The bottom-right Download icon already exists in Alva’s Home Screen footer.

Relevant files:

* js/screens/home-screen.js
* css/home.css
* js/ui/icons.js
* js/ui/overlays.js
* js/core/app.js
* index.html
* js/localization/strings/en.js
* js/localization/strings/fr.js

The button currently has disabled: true and no installation behavior.

Enable it and make it fully functional.

Keep its existing footer location, icon identity, button proportions, and overall design language.

3.2 Show an installation dialog

Clicking the bottom-right Download button must open an attractive, compact dialog explaining that Alva can be added to the player’s home screen and launched like an application.

Suggested English copy:

Title: Install Alva

Description:

“Want quicker access to Alva?

You can add Alva directly to your home screen and launch it just like an app, without opening your browser and searching for the game every time.

Alva is a lightweight web app, so there’s no large game download or traditional app installation required. It uses very little additional storage.

Add Alva to your home screen for a faster, more convenient way to play!”

Primary action:

Add to Home Screen

Secondary action:

Not Now

Maintain the existing dark, glass-inspired dialog styling.

The interface should feel like a natural part of Alva, not a generic browser alert.

Storage accuracy: A web app may still use some device storage for browser data, icons, or cached files. Do not make a technically false guarantee of literally zero storage. Emphasize that no large conventional app download is required and that the installation is lightweight.

3.3 Integrate with the existing dialog system

Reuse the architecture established by:

* ModalDialog
* InfoDialog
* ChoiceDialog
* The application’s menu navigation scopes

A dedicated install dialog is appropriate because it needs both explanatory content and an actionable installation button.

Requirements:

* Keyboard support.
* Controller/gamepad navigation.
* Touch compatibility.
* Appropriate dialog role and accessible title.
* Correct focus trapping and focus restoration.
* Escape and controller Back support.
* Closing the dialog must return focus to the Download button.
* Existing Home Screen functionality must remain available after dismissal.
* All displayed text must support Alva’s localization system.

Do not use browser alert() or confirm() as the main UI.

3.4 Add proper Progressive Web App support

Make Alva installable as a Progressive Web App wherever supported.

The repository already has some related metadata in index.html, including mobile web-app and Apple web-app configuration.

Complete the installability setup.

Implement a web app manifest containing appropriate fields such as:

{
  "name": "Alva",
  "short_name": "Alva",
  "description": "A browser-based platform fighting game.",
  "start_url": "./",
  "scope": "./",
  "display": "standalone",
  "background_color": "#050506",
  "theme_color": "#050506",
  "icons": []
}

Populate the icons array with actual, valid icon files and dimensions.

Use Alva’s existing branding, preferably deriving the required icons from its existing favicon or logo artwork.

Do not introduce unrelated icon designs.

Use at least suitable 192×192 and 512×512 icons, with appropriate formats and purposes where supported.

Link the manifest from index.html.

Alva may be deployed under a GitHub Pages repository subpath, so ensure manifest URLs, scope, start URL, icons, and other asset references resolve correctly without assuming the site is hosted at the domain root.

If a service worker is needed for the chosen installability and offline strategy, implement it carefully.

Do not introduce aggressive asset caching that causes unnecessarily high storage usage or stale game versions.

Offline gameplay is not an explicit requirement of this update. Prioritize reliable installation, ordinary online gameplay, and lightweight storage usage.

3.5 Native one-click installation where supported

Implement the browser’s native installation flow using supported web APIs.

On browsers that expose beforeinstallprompt:

1. Listen for the installability event.
2. Retain the event for a user-initiated installation.
3. Open the Alva installation dialog when the user clicks Download.
4. When the player presses Add to Home Screen, trigger the browser’s native installation prompt.
5. Let the browser display its own install confirmation.
6. Handle acceptance or dismissal appropriately.
7. Detect successful installation using appinstalled and update the interface.

The native installation prompt must be triggered in response to a real user interaction.

Do not attempt to bypass the browser’s permission or confirmation flow.

Do not falsely report that installation succeeded until the browser indicates success.

3.6 Unsupported browsers and iOS behavior

Some browsers, including Safari on iPhone and iPad, do not support the same programmable installation prompt.

The Download button must still be functional.

If direct installation is unavailable, display clear instructions rather than silently failing.

For Safari on iPhone or iPad, explain:

“To add Alva to your Home Screen:

1. Open Alva in Safari.
2. Tap the Share button.
3. Select Add to Home Screen.
4. Confirm by tapping Add.”

For supported desktop browsers without a programmable prompt, guide the player to the browser’s Install App or Add to Home Screen menu option where available.

Adapt these instructions to the browser and platform when reasonably detectable.

Do not claim that every device supports one-tap installation.

3.7 Detect when Alva is already installed

Handle a player opening Alva as an installed web app.

Use supported installation-state signals, such as:

* display-mode: standalone
* navigator.standalone where applicable
* appinstalled when available

If Alva is already running as an installed app, avoid showing another installation prompt.

Instead, the Download dialog can display a friendly message such as:

Alva is already installed!

“You can launch Alva directly from your Home Screen.”

Keep the interface consistent and ensure this state does not disable unrelated Home Screen features.

